Make diff exit with status 2 on every error, not only a missing operand.
diff set its error status to 2 only while it checked that the operands
exist, and to 1 before and after. So an invalid option or number, a
file missing from the directory when one operand is a directory, stdin
compared with a directory, or a temporary file that couldn't be created
all gave status 1, the status for "files differ", and a script couldn't
tell an error from a difference. diffutils exits with 2 for all of
these. Set the error status to 2 at the start and leave it there.

---
 editors/diff.c |    5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -1028,6 +1028,8 @@
 	char *file[2], *s_start = NULL;
 	llist_t *L_arg = NULL;
 
+	/* Like diffutils, exit with 2 on any error, as 1 means "differ" */
+	xfunc_error_retval = 2;
 	INIT_G();
 
 	/* exactly 2 params; collect multiple -L <label>; -U N */
@@ -1038,8 +1040,6 @@
 	while (L_arg)
 		label[!!label[0]] = llist_pop(&L_arg);
 
-	/* Compat: "diff file name_which_doesnt_exist" exits with 2 */
-	xfunc_error_retval = 2;
 	for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
 		file[i] = argv[i];
 		if (LONE_DASH(file[i])) {
@@ -1052,7 +1052,6 @@
 			xstat(file[i], &stb[i]);
 		}
 	}
-	xfunc_error_retval = 1;
 
 	if (gotstdin && (S_ISDIR(stb[0].st_mode) || S_ISDIR(stb[1].st_mode)))
 		bb_simple_error_msg_and_die("can't compare stdin to a directory");
